## Title: Daseeki Chat
## Notes: A modern, configurable chat window for WoW Classic Era with an account-spanning, mesh-synced chat configuration. Requires Daseeki-Core.
## Author: Daseeki
## Category: Chat & Communication
## X-License: All Rights Reserved
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1648776
## Dependencies: Daseeki-Core
## OptionalDeps: Daseeki-Nexus
## Interface: 11507, 11508, 11509
## Version: 0.9.0
## SavedVariables: DaseekiChatDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: DaseekiChatCharDB
#
# NOTE: prose comments in a .toc must use a SINGLE #. A ## prefix is a DIRECTIVE
# to the client's parser — the original ##-prefixed comment block below made the
# client read "## DEPENDENCIES — … (the Bags N1 lesson): every" as a dependency
# on an addon named "every", and the whole addon refused to load (live incident,
# 2026-08-10, caught in BugSack on first UAT).
#
# SAVEDVARIABLES CONTRACT (the Bags AT-RISK-1 lesson applies from day one): the
# client rewrites this addon's SavedVariables files at every logout from the
# DECLARED names only — a global dropped from these lines is erased at the next
# logout, silently. Two stores, deliberately split:
#   DaseekiChatDB     — the authoritative account-spanning chat CONFIG (windows,
#                       tabs, routing, colors, fonts, layout) plus module flags.
#                       This is what the reconciler treats as truth and what the
#                       Nexus `chatcfg` namespace syncs. Account-wide by design.
#   DaseekiChatCharDB — per-character, high-churn, never synced: cross-session
#                       chat HISTORY snapshots and any per-character debug traces.
#                       Isolated so config sync never drags scrollback around
#                       (the Prat "high CPU file" precedent).
#
# DEPENDENCIES — Daseeki-Core is HARD and honest (the Bags N1 lesson): every
# visual surface here is drawn from Core theme tokens and Core font roles; there
# is no Core-less rendering path. Daseeki-Nexus stays OPTIONAL and must NOT be
# promoted: nexus.lua is fully type-guarded and Chat is unchanged without it —
# the OptionalDeps line is a LOAD-ORDER statement only (Nexus SavedVariables must
# be attached before our ADDON_LOADED so the chatcfg adopt decision can see them).
#
# FILE MAP (DASEEKI_CHAT_DESIGN.md is LAW; this list is its file map, in order).
# Wave ownership: Wave 1 built core.lua + skin.lua + this skeleton + the harness.
# Three Wave-2 agents fill the placeholders IN PLACE — the .toc never changes and
# no agent touches another agent's files:
#   reconciler/sync agent : config.lua, reconcile.lua, channels.lua, nexus.lua
#   pipeline agent        : decor.lua, stamps.lua, names.lua, urls.lua
#   history/badges agent  : history.lua, badges.lua
core.lua
# config.lua: the authoritative config model + capture-back diffing. Loads right
# after core because every other module reads config at call time.
config.lua
# reconcile.lua: the login/entering-world reconciler (the flagship). Event-gated
# on the ENTERING_WORLD bus message core fires; never timer-guessed (Class 2).
reconcile.lua
# channels.lua: channel membership + deterministic numbering + color-by-name
# re-imposition. All server round-trips paced >=0.5s with verify-and-retry.
channels.lua
# decor.lua: the message pipeline — protect-tokenize-restore engine. Hyperlink/|K
# protection is UNCONDITIONAL, never coupled to another feature (the Prat
# coupling bug is the anti-lesson).
decor.lua
stamps.lua
names.lua
urls.lua
# history.lua: cross-session history — ring-buffer snapshot at logout, server-time
# stamping, restamp-on-restore (uptime-based entries fade instantly otherwise).
history.lua
badges.lua
# skin.lua: frame/editbox/tab restyle per suite theme + the copy-chat affordance.
# Loads after every pipeline module so its module registration order (and the
# /dchat debug registry) lists engine before dress.
skin.lua
# options.lua: the settings pane (Daseeki-Core hub page) + the channel-alias
# editor. FILE MAP AMENDMENT, post-V1, owner-requested 2026-08-11 ("do we not
# have a configuration menu for chat?") — DASEEKI_CHAT_DESIGN.md's file map and
# the harness's EXPECTED_FILE_MAP gate were amended in the same commit; the gate
# still pins this list byte-for-byte. Loads AFTER every module it configures
# (it binds against their published default shapes) and BEFORE nexus.lua, which
# only bridges what config.lua already owns.
options.lua
# nexus.lua: the OPTIONAL Daseeki-Nexus chatcfg bridge. ZERO hard dependency:
# every call is type-guarded; Chat is unchanged without Nexus. Last on the list
# because it only bridges what config.lua already owns.
nexus.lua
